From be65e08c1873541932b43938858aa8d50a5efc41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Romain Beauxis <romain.beauxis@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:45:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/mov: ignore discarded streams when placing the
 fragment position on seek

With seek_individually, the last stream seeked sets next_root_atom, so a chapter track whose samples all sit in the first fragment makes mov_read_packet() read every fragment from the start of the file before it reaches the seeked sample.

Resume reading from the earliest fragment any stream that is read landed in, which keeps the fragments that a lagging audio track still needs and ignores the chapter track.

The seek in fate-mov-mp4-frag-chapters-seek no longer restarts from the beginning of the file.

[Hades: backport to 9.1 without tests/ref/fate/mov-mp4-frag-chapters-seek: FATE files of tests that master added after 9.1 (or, for libavformat/tests/.gitignore, a file the release tarball does not have).]

(cherry picked from commit be65e08c1873541932b43938858aa8d50a5efc41)
Upstream: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/be65e08c1873541932b43938858aa8d50a5efc41
---
 libavformat/mov.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavformat/mov.c b/libavformat/mov.c
index 597c0aa..5684498 100644
--- a/libavformat/mov.c
+++ b/libavformat/mov.c
@@ -13226,21 +13226,31 @@ static int mov_read_seek(AVFormatContext *s, int stream_index, int64_t sample_ti
     if (mc->seek_individually) {
         /* adjust seek timestamp to found sample timestamp */
         int64_t seek_timestamp = sti->index_entries[sample].timestamp;
+        int64_t next_root_atom = mc->next_root_atom;
         sti->skip_samples = mov_get_skip_samples(st, sample);
 
         for (i = 0; i < s->nb_streams; i++) {
             AVStream *const st  = s->streams[i];
             FFStream *const sti = ffstream(st);
+            const MOVStreamContext *sc = st->priv_data;
             int64_t timestamp;
 
             if (stream_index == i)
                 continue;
 
+            mc->next_root_atom = 0;
             timestamp = av_rescale_q(seek_timestamp, s->streams[stream_index]->time_base, st->time_base);
             sample = mov_seek_stream(s, st, timestamp, flags);
             if (sample >= 0)
                 sti->skip_samples = mov_get_skip_samples(st, sample);
+
+            /* Reading resumes from the earliest fragment a read stream landed
+             * in; a discarded chapter track would send it back to the start. */
+            if ((st->discard != AVDISCARD_ALL || sc->iamf) && mc->next_root_atom &&
+                (!next_root_atom || mc->next_root_atom < next_root_atom))
+                next_root_atom = mc->next_root_atom;
         }
+        mc->next_root_atom = next_root_atom;
     } else {
         for (i = 0; i < s->nb_streams; i++) {
             MOVStreamContext *sc;
